## Trade-offs

### ✅ Advantages

| Aspect | Benefit |
|--------|---------|
| **Hot path performance** | Zero overhead (no Python, just JSONL append) |
| **Robustness** | Graceful degradation - evolution works without neuro-memory |
| **Debuggability** | Single process invocation, easy to inspect |
| **Batch efficiency** | Bayesian surprise computed on thousands of events at once |
| **Full history** | Can analyze patterns across weeks, not just last 10 events |
| **Simplicity** | No message queues, no long-running Python process, no sockets |

### ⚠️ Disadvantages

| Aspect | Mitigation |
|--------|------------|
| **Startup latency** | Python VM startup (~500ms) - acceptable for weekly run |
| **Memory usage** | Loading 30 days of events - keep events small, or use SQLite |
| **No real-time insights** | Acceptable - evolution doesn't need real-time |
| **Event store grows** | Add rotation/compaction (keep last 90 days) |

